  "story": "Ember was a friendly dragon who tended a magical forest. She watered seedlings and listened to the mushrooms’ stories. One morning, an old map appeared beneath her favorite stone, marking lost treasure beyond the winding silver stream.\n\nThe map promised something precious enough to help the whole forest. Ember packed a basket of berries and followed its dotted path. Every glowing mushroom seemed to lean closer, curious about where the adventure would lead.\n\nEmber tried crossing the silver stream on stepping stones. She moved slowly, balancing her basket and tail. Halfway across, she heard a tiny cry. A turtle was trapped beneath a branch near the rushing water.\n\nThe last stone slipped underwater, and Ember could not reach the turtle safely. Her map floated away, but she let it go. Treasure could wait. She needed a better way to help without sweeping them both downstream.\n\nEmber spotted a fallen log and gently laid it across the stream. The turtle climbed to safety, then showed her a shallow path. At its end, Ember found a healing crystal, the forest’s lost treasure.\n\nBack home, Ember used the crystal to heal a wounded mushroom. The turtle visited often, and the map dried beside the fire. Ember smiled at her sparkling forest, knowing kindness had guided her better than any dotted line.",
  "main_characters": [
    {
      "name": "Ember",
      "description": "A friendly dragon with emerald scales, amber eyes, rounded wings, a cream belly, four short legs and a tail with soft green spikes."
    }
  ],
  "scenes": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "beat": "setup",
      "title": "The Forest Guardian",
      "description": "Ember watering seedlings among glowing mushrooms in a magical forest.",
      "characters": [
        "Ember"
      ],
      "text": "Ember was a friendly dragon who tended a magical forest. She watered seedlings and listened to the mushrooms’ stories. One morning, an old map appeared beneath her favorite stone, marking lost treasure beyond the winding silver stream."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "beat": "inciting_incident",
      "title": "The Map’s Promise",
      "description": "Ember studying the treasure map beside a glowing mushroom.",
      "characters": [
        "Ember"
      ],
      "text": "The map promised something precious enough to help the whole forest. Ember packed a basket of berries and followed its dotted path. Every glowing mushroom seemed to lean closer, curious about where the adventure would lead."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "beat": "first_attempt",
      "title": "Across the Stepping Stones",
      "description": "Ember crossing stepping stones over a silver stream with a berry basket.",
      "characters": [
        "Ember"
      ],
      "text": "Ember tried crossing the silver stream on stepping stones. She moved slowly, balancing her basket and tail. Halfway across, she heard a tiny cry. A turtle was trapped beneath a branch near the rushing water."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "beat": "setback",
      "title": "The Missing Stone",
      "description": "Ember reaching toward the turtle as a stepping stone slips underwater.",
      "characters": [
        "Ember"
      ],
      "text": "The last stone slipped underwater, and Ember could not reach the turtle safely. Her map floated away, but she let it go. Treasure could wait. She needed a better way to help without sweeping them both downstream."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "beat": "climax",
      "title": "A Bridge of Kindness",
      "description": "Ember laying a fallen log across the stream for the turtle.",
      "characters": [
        "Ember"
      ],
      "text": "Ember spotted a fallen log and gently laid it across the stream. The turtle climbed to safety, then showed her a shallow path. At its end, Ember found a healing crystal, the forest’s lost treasure."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "beat": "resolution",
      "title": "The Greatest Treasure",
      "description": "Ember healing a wounded mushroom with the crystal while the turtle watches.",
      "characters": [
        "Ember"
      ],
      "text": "Back home, Ember used the crystal to heal a wounded mushroom. The turtle visited often, and the map dried beside the fire. Ember smiled at her sparkling forest, knowing kindness had guided her better than any dotted line."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "story": "Pip swept leaves along a rainy city sidewalk while Marmalade watched from a dry windowsill. The little robot liked tidy paths, and the kitten liked company. Every evening, they waited for the bakery to open.\n\nTonight, a golden blink appeared behind a recycling bin. Pip wondered whether someone had dropped a lantern. Marmalade stepped down, and together they rolled and padded into the alley to investigate the mysterious light.\n\nThey found a firefly trapped behind a puddle. Pip offered a folded leaf as a bridge, and Marmalade held it steady with both paws. The firefly crawled closer, glowing hopefully toward the dry pavement.\n\nThen a fat raindrop splashed down. The leaf tipped, and the firefly slipped backward. Pip's wheels skidded, but he caught the stem. Marmalade crouched beside him, thinking carefully instead of rushing into the water.\n\nMarmalade spotted a broad piece of bark. She anchored one end while Pip lifted the other into place. Their wider bridge stayed still, and the firefly stepped across. Pip cheered so loudly his scarf fluttered.\n\nThe baker welcomed all three beneath her awning. Marmalade curled beside Pip, and the firefly glowed above them like a tiny star. The path could wait until morning; helping a new friend had made tonight perfect.",
  "main_characters": [
    {
      "name": "Pip",
      "description": "A small round silver robot, basketball-sized, with one cyan circular eye, two short arms with three-fingered hands, four tiny black wheels, and a red scarf tied on the left side."
    },
    {
      "name": "Marmalade",
      "description": "A tiny orange tabby kitten with three dark stripes on each cheek, four white paws, round green eyes, a pink nose and a cream-tipped tail."
    }
  ],
  "scenes": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "beat": "setup",
      "title": "A Rainy Round",
      "description": "Pip and Marmalade beside a leaf-covered city sidewalk at dusk, rain shining under amber streetlights.",
      "characters": [
        "Pip",
        "Marmalade"
      ],
      "text": "Pip swept leaves along a rainy city sidewalk while Marmalade watched from a dry windowsill. The little robot liked tidy paths, and the kitten liked company. Every evening, they waited for the bakery to open."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "beat": "inciting_incident",
      "title": "A Light in the Alley",
      "description": "Pip noticing a faint golden glow behind a recycling bin in a narrow alley; Marmalade peering around the corner.",
      "characters": [
        "Pip",
        "Marmalade"
      ],
      "text": "Tonight, a golden blink appeared behind a recycling bin. Pip wondered whether someone had dropped a lantern. Marmalade stepped down, and together they rolled and padded into the alley to investigate the mysterious light."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "beat": "first_attempt",
      "title": "The Leaf Bridge",
      "description": "Pip extending an arm toward a small glowing firefly trapped behind a puddle, using a folded leaf as a bridge while Marmalade holds it steady.",
      "characters": [
        "Pip",
        "Marmalade"
      ],
      "text": "They found a firefly trapped behind a puddle. Pip offered a folded leaf as a bridge, and Marmalade held it steady with both paws. The firefly crawled closer, glowing hopefully toward the dry pavement."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "beat": "setback",
      "title": "A Splash and a Slide",
      "description": "A raindrop splashing into the puddle and tipping the leaf bridge; Pip bracing the leaf while Marmalade reaches for the firefly.",
      "characters": [
        "Pip",
        "Marmalade"
      ],
      "text": "Then a fat raindrop splashed down. The leaf tipped, and the firefly slipped backward. Pip's wheels skidded, but he caught the stem. Marmalade crouched beside him, thinking carefully instead of rushing into the water."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "beat": "climax",
      "title": "A Better Way Across",
      "description": "Marmalade anchoring a broad piece of bark while Pip lifts it into a stable bridge; the firefly stepping safely onto dry pavement.",
      "characters": [
        "Pip",
        "Marmalade"
      ],
      "text": "Marmalade spotted a broad piece of bark. She anchored one end while Pip lifted the other into place. Their wider bridge stayed still, and the firefly stepped across. Pip cheered so loudly his scarf fluttered."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "beat": "resolution",
      "title": "Warmth for Three",
      "description": "Pip, Marmalade and the freed firefly resting beneath the bakery awning, warm bread visible in the window and the rain easing.",
      "characters": [
        "Pip",
        "Marmalade"
      ],
      "text": "The baker welcomed all three beneath her awning. Marmalade curled beside Pip, and the firefly glowed above them like a tiny star. The path could wait until morning; helping a new friend had made tonight perfect."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "story": "Luna was a butterfly who knew every corner of a colorful garden. She visited the daisies each morning and rested beside the fence at noon. Her violet wings made the children smile whenever she fluttered past.\n\nOne hot morning, the flowers drooped and bees gathered around an empty watering can. Luna wondered why the gardener had not visited. She followed the path to the gate and found it stuck against a stone.\n\nLuna tried moving the pebble with all her weight. It did not budge. Then she pushed a smaller seed, hoping to make a path for water. The seed rolled away, but the garden stayed thirsty.\n\nA hot wind bent the flowers, and Luna sheltered beneath a leaf. She felt too small to help. Then she noticed children watching from the other side of the gate, waiting for someone to show them trouble.\n\nLuna flew above the gate, then dipped toward the pebble again and again. The children followed her, moved the stone, and opened the path. They carried watering cans between the rows while Luna guided them to the driest flowers.\n\nBy evening, the garden lifted its bright faces. Bees hummed, children laughed, and Luna danced above the daisies. She had not moved the stone herself, but her tiny wings had shown everyone where help was needed.",
